<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tej Singh Prabhakar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1911">1911</a>–<a href="/years/2009">2009</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tej Singh of Alwar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tej Singh Prabhakar was the last ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Alwar, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> princely state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, succeeding in 1937. He acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> after independence in 1947, and in March 1948 Alwar was merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matsya-union">Matsya Union</a>, of which it became the capital. In 1949 the union joined the United State of Rajasthan.</p></div>
